# AGC Specification Rules

## Feature Context

The GitHub Issue being processed is the authoritative
source for the current feature request.

Do not use another feature's spec, plan, or tasks as
the current feature context.

## Brownfield Context

For specification work, inspect relevant existing
documentation and implementation before making
architectural assumptions:

- /docs/sdd-brownfield/
- /specs/project-context/
- /specs/baseline-system/
- /src/

Verify documented behavior against the current
implementation.

If documentation and implementation disagree,
document the discrepancy.

## Requirements

Preserve confirmed:

- business rules
- acceptance criteria
- security requirements
- integration boundaries
- existing system constraints

Do not invent requirements or architecture.

## Feature Isolation

The specification must be created under the directory
corresponding to the current F1.xx feature.

Do not modify another feature's specification, plan,
or task files.

## Hooks

Allow configured Spec Kit extension hooks to execute
after specification generation.

Do not manually duplicate an automatically enabled hook.